<title>USA: Some Pizza Huts violated child labor law-NYT.</title>
<headline>Some Pizza Huts violated child labor law-NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal government said 26 Pizza Hut restaurants in the New York area violated child labor laws by letting youths operate dangerous equipment like slicing machines, the New York Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Department of Labor fined the company, owned by PepsiCo, $194,400 in civil penalties, the paper said.</p>
<p>Federal law forbids people under 18 to operate dough mixers and rollers or electric slicers, the paper said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
